From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 02:01:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] liblog: getprogname from the C library when built for Android

logger_write.cpp defines its own static getprogname() for every C
library but bionic and Apple's. A device build against another C
library that provides bionic's API declares getprogname() in
<stdlib.h> under __ANDROID__, so the static definition follows an
extern declaration and fails to compile. Skip it under __ANDROID__
too. No change for Soong variants: device builds define __BIONIC__.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [no Soong variant defines __ANDROID__ without __BIONIC__]
Patch-Reason: the definition is compiled inside liblog's source, out of reach of the launcher, loader and environment; ART calls bionic's getprogname under __ANDROID__ (oat_file_manager.cc), so the declaration must stay in <stdlib.h>
---
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 liblog/logger_write.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/liblog/logger_write.cpp b/liblog/logger_write.cpp
index 4f596043795475c1f68b8c0aa8f9860b7957ba5e..7eff2af23f71d6fa9f22bc2ec62aab8b8b360382 100644
--- a/liblog/logger_write.cpp
+++ b/liblog/logger_write.cpp
@@ -120,7 +120,7 @@ void __android_log_close() {
 }
 
 // BSD-based systems like Android/macOS have getprogname(). Others need us to provide one.
-#if !defined(__APPLE__) && !defined(__BIONIC__)
+#if !defined(__APPLE__) && !defined(__BIONIC__) && !defined(__ANDROID__)
 static const char* getprogname() {
 #ifdef _WIN32
   static bool first = true;
